id: SECRETS-073
title: Elastic API Key
category: secrets
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .tsx .js .jsx .py .java .go .rb .rs .cpp .h .cs .php .env .yml .yaml .json .toml .xml .properties .cfg .ini .conf .sh .tf .hcl
  exclude_paths: test/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/ __pycache__/ .venv/ target/
  content_contains: elastic
patterns:
  - regex: [a-zA-Z0-9_-]{20}:[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{20}
    message: Elasticsearch API key detected. This grants access to indices, documents, and cluster operations.
fix: Invalidate the key via the Elasticsearch API (`_security/api_key`). Create a new key with minimal role descriptors and store in environment variables.
